.TH CLEAN-PORTS 1 "October 2026" "devtools-hub 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clean-ports \- inspect and deterministically terminate processes bound to a TCP port
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clean-ports
.I port
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clean-ports
queries active network sockets via
.BR lsof (8)
to identify processes listening on the specified TCP
.I port
and terminates them gracefully using
.B SIGTERM
with fallback to
.BR SIGKILL .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print active PIDs bound to the target port without sending termination signals.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Target port was freed successfully, was already free, or dry-run completed.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments or non-numeric port specification.
